{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
At [Bb]that time Mic[Eb]hael shall a[F]rise
[Eb]The great [Bb/D]prince who stands [F]guard
Over [Gm]your peo[Eb]ple in the [Bb/D]dust
In a [Cm7]time of [Eb]great dis[Bb]tress
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Some to [Eb]ever[F]lasting [Bb]life
Some to [Eb]shame [F]and con[Gm]tempt
But the wise shall [Eb]shine
Like [F]the brightness of the firma[Bb]ment
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Those whose names are [Eb]in the [F]book
Will [Eb]be de[Bb/D]livered [F]then
[Gm]Sleeping in [Eb]the dust of [Bb/D]earth
A[Cm7]wakening [F7sus4]once a[Bb]gain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Some to [Eb]ever[F]lasting [Bb]life
Some to [Eb]shame [F]and con[Gm]tempt
But the wise [Gm7/F]shall [Eb]shine
Like [F]the brightness of the firma[Bb]ment
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Lead many to right[F]eousness
Like the [Bb]stars forever and ev[Gm7]er
[Eb]Shining bright in the [F]sky
Your re[Gm]ward is forever
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Some to [Eb]ever[F]lasting [Bb]life
Some to [Eb]shame [F]and con[Gm]tempt
